from scoper.harness.control_prompts import MEMORY_SYSTEM_BYTES as MEMORY_V18, POLICY_SYSTEM_BYTES as POLICY_V18
from scoper.harness.control_prompts import VERIFIER_SYSTEM_BYTES as VERIFIER_V18
from scoper.harness.compatibility import QWEN35_POLICY_D4_GUIDANCE_SUFFIX_BYTES
GRIPPER_MARKER_GUIDANCE_BYTES = b'Robot appearance: when present, the green/cyan sphere attached to the robot gripper is a simulator visualization marker, not a task object. Ignore that sphere and the robot arm/gripper when identifying objects or deciding whether an object is held. The marker remains visible with an empty hand; its presence never proves pickup or continued holding. Require a separately identifiable task object, distinct from the marker and gripper. Do not ignore real green objects elsewhere in the scene. If that distinction is unclear, report uncertainty instead of claiming an object is held. Prior memory descriptions do not override the current RGB evidence.\n'
POLICY_SYSTEM_BYTES = POLICY_V18.replace(b'phase=retry or phase=final_retry requires failed_tool_call with exactly the saved tool_name and arguments.', b'For non-placement recovery, phase=retry or phase=final_retry requires the saved failed_tool_call. For put_down recovery, obey the currently exposed tool schema and locked target instead: the controller may require observing, navigating to the carried object, picking it up, or returning to the destination before retrying placement.').replace(b'If put_down fails or the object is no longer held, stop retrying put_down: reacquire the object with navigate_to then pick_up, verify that it is held, and only then retry put_down.', b'After a failed put_down, old held evidence is stale. If RGB confirms release, reacquire the object with navigate_to then pick_up, then navigate_to the destination and retry put_down. If fresh RGB confirms it is still held, repair destination readiness and retry directly. Recovery pickup may supply an uncertain planning-only held assumption for one placement attempt; it is not verified holding or task success. Follow the required recovery call even if pickup RGB is unclear. If unclear, use the single bounded observation requested by recovery; never guess inventory.') + GRIPPER_MARKER_GUIDANCE_BYTES
MEMORY_SYSTEM_BYTES = MEMORY_V18 + b'For a task-relevant placement object, prioritize visible hand status in observe mode. Use the same concrete public name as in prior memory. When RGB clearly shows the object in the hand, begin its scene_observation text with "Visibly held in hand:" and a short visual description. When RGB clearly shows that object resting outside the hand, begin with "Visibly outside hand:" and its visible location. If the object or hand status is unclear, omit these prefixes. Missing objects and an empty-looking crop alone do not prove release. A requested put_down, failed verification, or recovery instruction is never evidence of release.\n' + GRIPPER_MARKER_GUIDANCE_BYTES
VERIFIER_SYSTEM_BYTES = VERIFIER_V18 + GRIPPER_MARKER_GUIDANCE_BYTES
D6_POLICY_SYSTEM_BYTES = POLICY_SYSTEM_BYTES + QWEN35_POLICY_D4_GUIDANCE_SUFFIX_BYTES.replace(b'Follow the public recovery field exactly: perform its required preparation or saved ToolCall before returning to the task.', b'Follow the current allowed_tool_specs and locked argument values exactly. For put_down recovery they may require reacquiring the object before the saved placement ToolCall; this exception takes precedence over generic original-action retry instructions.')
